Jack: It really was. I love that he photographed ordinary people, not just famous stars.
Emma: Yes. The guide said he rode the same old bicycle around New York for years.
Jack: And he always wore that simple blue jacket. He cared nothing for money.
Emma: My favourite part was that he went out every day, even in the rain.
Jack: Mine too. The photo of a woman on a snowy street felt so alive.
Emma: I think his secret was patience. He waited for the perfect moment.
Jack: Exactly. After today, I really want to try street photography myself.', 'Emma 和 Jack 看完 Bill Cunningham 的街拍摄影展;他拍普通人而非明星;骑同一辆旧自行车、总穿蓝外套、不在乎钱;每天出门拍照,即使下雨;Jack 觉得雪天街上女子的照片很生动;Emma 认为他的秘诀是耐心、等待最佳时机;Jack 看完想自己尝试街拍。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What kind of exhibition did Emma and Jack see?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Bill Cunningham''s street photographs.","A show of old oil paintings.","A display of ancient maps.","A collection of film posters."]},{"q":"Who did Cunningham mainly photograph?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only world-famous singers.","Ordinary people, not only famous stars.","Animals in the city park.","Tall new buildings."]},{"q":"What did Cunningham wear every day?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A simple blue jacket.","A bright red coat.","An expensive black suit.","A white uniform."]},{"q":"When did he still go out to take photos?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only on sunny weekends.","Every day, even in the rain.","Just once a month.","Only at night."]},{"q":"What does Jack want to do after the visit?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Buy a very expensive camera.","Open his own art gallery.","Try street photography himself.","Stop taking photos for good."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Every morning he chooses a block of soft wood and shapes it slowly by hand.
Making a single pair of wooden shoes can take him a whole day.
He says machines could do it faster, but they could never give each pair its own character.
Few young people want to learn the craft today, because it is hard and pays little.
Still, he keeps a small workshop open and teaches anyone who is truly interested.
He hopes the old skill will not disappear with him.', '一个小镇上住着最后几位传统木鞋匠之一。他每天清晨挑一块软木,慢慢用手雕成。做一双木鞋要花他一整天。他说机器更快,却给不了每双鞋独特的个性。如今很少有年轻人愿学这门又难又挣钱少的手艺。但他仍开着小作坊,教任何真心想学的人,希望这门老手艺不会随他消失。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the man make?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Glass bottles.","Paper umbrellas.","Metal tools.","Traditional wooden shoes."]},{"q":"How long can one pair take him?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["About a whole day.","Only a few minutes.","Exactly one week.","Less than an hour."]},{"q":"Why does he prefer handwork to machines?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Machines are far too cheap.","Each pair gains its own character.","He has never seen a machine.","Machines make the shoes too strong."]},{"q":"Why do few young people learn the craft?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is against the law.","It can only be done at night.","It is hard and earns little money.","It needs very expensive tools."]},{"q":"What does he hope for the future?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["That machines will replace him.","That the workshop will close.","That prices will rise sharply.","That the skill will not die out."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Lily: Thank you. I started by simply watching people on the street for hours.
Host: Interesting. So observation came before the camera?
Lily: Yes. My teacher said a photographer must first learn to see.
Host: What do you enjoy photographing most?
Lily: Small everyday moments, like an old man feeding birds in the park.
Host: Do you use expensive equipment?
Lily: Not at all. Light and patience matter far more than a costly camera.
Host: That''s wonderful advice. Thank you, Lily.', '主持人采访年轻摄影师 Lily。她说自己最初是花几小时观察街上的人;观察先于相机;老师说摄影师必须先学会观察;她最爱拍日常小瞬间,比如公园里喂鸟的老人;她不用昂贵器材,认为光线和耐心远比贵相机重要;主持人称赞这是很好的建议。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How did Lily begin learning photography?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["By watching people for hours.","By buying the newest camera.","By copying famous photos.","By taking a long holiday."]},{"q":"What did her teacher say she must learn first?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To run a busy studio.","To observe carefully, or to see.","To sell her photos quickly.","To use bright stage lights."]},{"q":"What does Lily most enjoy photographing?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Tall mountains far away.","Famous film stars.","Small everyday moments.","New cars and machines."]},{"q":"What does Lily say matters more than a costly camera?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Money and fame.","A large team of helpers.","A warm indoor studio.","Light and patience."]},{"q":"What is the host''s opinion of Lily''s advice?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He thinks it is wonderful.","He finds it rather silly.","He completely disagrees.","He is not interested."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
For a while, fewer and fewer people practised it, and many feared it would be forgotten.
Recently, however, the art has become popular again.
Schools now invite old artists to teach children how to cut delicate flowers and animals from red paper.
Online videos of skilled artisans have been watched by millions of people.
Many say they enjoy the calm, careful nature of the work in such a busy world.
Thanks to this new interest, an ancient craft is finding fresh life.', '剪纸是中国最古老的民间艺术之一。曾有一阵子练习的人越来越少,许多人担心它会被遗忘。然而最近这门艺术又流行起来。学校请老艺人教孩子用红纸剪出精致的花鸟;技艺高超的艺人的网络视频被数百万人观看;很多人说在忙碌的世界里喜欢这种平静而专注的工作。多亏这股新兴趣,一门古老手艺正焕发新生。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What folk art does the passage describe?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Wood painting.","Paper-cutting.","Stone building.","Glass blowing."]},{"q":"What happened to the art for a while?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It was banned by law.","It became too expensive.","Fewer people practised it.","It was only done abroad."]},{"q":"How are schools helping the art today?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They sell red paper to shops.","They print it in textbooks only.","They keep it a secret from children.","They invite old artists to teach children."]},{"q":"Why have online videos mattered?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Millions of people have watched skilled artisans.","They taught machines to cut paper.","They warned people to stop the art.","They were watched by no one."]},{"q":"Why do many people enjoy the work?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It makes them rich very fast.","It is calm and careful in a busy world.","It is loud and exciting.","It needs no skill at all."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Visitor: They''re beautiful! Where did they come from?
Guide: Many were gifts to Chinese emperors from foreign envoys long ago.
Visitor: How are such old clocks kept working?
Guide: A few skilled masters repair them, but each one takes months of work.
Visitor: Months? That sounds incredibly slow.
Guide: It must be slow. Every tiny part has to be cleaned and fixed by hand.
Visitor: When a clock chimes, it must feel like magic.
Guide: It does. To the masters, that sound is the finest music in the world.', '讲解员带访客参观博物馆里最古老的钟表。许多钟是古时外国使节献给中国皇帝的;少数技艺高超的师傅修理它们,但每件要花几个月;访客觉得很慢;讲解员说必须慢,每个小部件都要手工清洁、修复;钟报时时仿佛魔法;对师傅们来说,那声音是世上最美的音乐。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does this museum room hold?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Modern phones and screens.","Old war weapons.","Some of the oldest clocks.","Famous paintings."]},{"q":"Where did many of the clocks come from?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A local toy factory.","Ordinary family homes.","A nearby school.","Gifts from foreign envoys to emperors."]},{"q":"How long can repairing one clock take?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Several months.","A few seconds.","Exactly one hour.","Less than a day."]},{"q":"Why is the work so slow?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The masters are very lazy.","Each part is cleaned and fixed by hand.","The clocks are made of paper.","There are too many visitors."]},{"q":"How do the masters feel about the chiming sound?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They find it very annoying.","They never listen to it.","They love it like the finest music.","They think it is too quiet."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Slow down and really look at the world around you.
The best pictures and the finest work do not come from expensive tools, but from patience and a careful eye.
Notice the small things that others walk past: the light on a wall, the lines on an old hand.
If you train yourself to see, ideas will come from everywhere.
Remember, a careful observer today can become a true artist tomorrow.', '给所有热爱摄影或任何手艺的人一个简单建议:慢下来,真正去看你周围的世界。最好的照片和最精的作品不来自昂贵器材,而来自耐心和细致的眼睛。留意别人匆匆走过的小事:墙上的光、老人手上的纹路。若你训练自己去观察,灵感会来自四面八方。记住,今天细心的观察者,明天可以成为真正的艺术家。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip mainly for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only professional athletes.","Only museum guides.","People who dislike art.","People who love photography or a craft."]},{"q":"What does the speaker tell listeners to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Slow down and look carefully.","Buy the newest equipment.","Work as fast as possible.","Copy other people''s photos."]},{"q":"Where does the finest work come from?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Expensive tools alone.","Patience and a careful eye.","Pure good luck.","A large, costly studio."]},{"q":"What small things should you notice?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only big, famous buildings.","Only bright stage lights.","Things others walk past, like light and lines.","Nothing at all."]},{"q":"What can a careful observer become?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A fast machine.","A famous singer.","A clock maker.","A true artist."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U2', 'fltrp');

